            <chunk name="Object" index="5">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e1a7d3b5-8c2f-4a69-b0d4-7f3e9c5a1b28</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">3f8d2b61-9c4e-4a07-b2d5-7e1a6c90f4b3</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Noise Run</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="6">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Road-traffic noise after CNOSSOS-EU (Directive 2015/996, 2021/1226 coefficients): the emission of every road and the propagation to every receiver — divergence, air absorption, the ground effect on the mean plane, diffraction over roofs and crests — summed per octave band and period into Lday, Levening, Lnight and Lden.

PROTOTYPE LIMITS: homogeneous atmospheric conditions only (no favourable-propagation share, so distant levels run a little low); no facade reflections; no path around a corner (a receiver behind a block gets the over-the-roof path only, which reads low); one ground factor for the whole site; no rail, aircraft or industry. Not a compliance calculation.

Method: CNOSSOS-EU, Commission Directive (EU) 2015/996 Annex II (road emission §2.2, propagation §2.5), coefficients per Delegated Directive (EU) 2021/1226, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2015/996/oj — pinned against NoiseModelling (Université Gustave Eiffel) on the ISO/TR 17534-4 cases.

